## Correctness decisions

1. Replace v1 item pointers with offsets into the same C-owned immutable arena.
   Call only `rn_verify_v2`, initialize its bitmap, and check each bit against
   its item status, rejecting bits outside the batch. Keep source and arena
   alive through native return, including cancellation. Mixed and 1/63/64-item
   tests confirm item-i/bit-i ordering, including bit 63 and variable offsets.
2. Store high/normal priority as admission metadata, excluded from the payload
   digest. Retries preserve the original priority. Rebuild FIFO queues in
   sequence order at startup, retaining schema 1 and all durable job information.
3. Advance the H,H,H,N cycle only when both runnable queues are nonempty.
   Prune cancelled queued entries before selection. Single-queue dispatch and
   idleness neither advance nor reset the cycle. Startup begins at H.
4. Review identified that predecessor workers selected jobs before waiting for
   shared native slots. That could preselect normal jobs while evaluations held
   all four slots. Selection now reserves an available slot under the state
   mutex. Evaluations wait on the same condition variable; native completion
   broadcasts availability. Native calls remain concurrent, outside the mutex.
5. Preserve one-job admission/terminal WriteBatches, sync/WAL, storage settings,
   exclusive locking, admission-ordered terminal commitment and the mutex that
   spans durable writes to protect cancellation ordering. No group commit.

